translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.bug_fixing	Diagnosing, troubleshooting, and resolving defects, errors, test failures, or unexpected behavior.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.ci_cd_and_devops	Setting up and maintaining CI/CD pipelines, deployment configurations, and infrastructure-as-code.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.code_review	Reviewing pull requests, analyzing code quality, and providing feedback on existing code.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.data_and_automation	Building data pipelines, scripts, and automation workflows for repetitive tasks.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.documentation_and_content	Writing or updating documentation, READMEs, changelogs, API docs, wikis, translations, localization (i18n/l10n), and content creation.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.feature_development	Building new features, implementing user stories, and adding new functionality to the codebase.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.migrations_and_upgrades	Upgrading dependencies, migrating frameworks, databases, or APIs to newer versions.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.other	Sessions that don’t fit neatly into the categories above.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.production_investigation	Diagnosing, troubleshooting, and resolving alerts or incidents in a production context.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.refactoring_and_optimization	Improving code structure, performance, and maintainability without changing external behavior.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.research_and_exploration	Exploring feasibility, researching solutions, investigating options, designing architecture, writing RFCs, planning, and prototyping.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.security	Fixing security vulnerabilities, addressing CVEs, and improving application security posture.
translation.sessionCategoryDescriptions.unit_test_generation	Writing unit tests, integration tests, and improving test coverage across the codebase.
